# Aql — local development env (repo root)
#
# Copy to .env:   cp .env.example .env
#
# Who reads this file:
#   - Vite (the portal): only VITE_-prefixed vars, and they are PUBLIC in the
#     browser bundle — never put a secret in one.
#   - The Go gateway reads LINTEL_* from its own environment, not from this
#     file. Run it as `AQL_DATA_DIR=./data go run ./cmd/hub`, or export
#     them in your shell. They are documented here for reference.
#
# The LINTEL_ prefix is deliberate. It is a deployment contract that predates
# the fold into Aql; renaming it would break every existing install for a
# cosmetic gain. gateway/README.md holds the authoritative table.

# ── The gateway (Go + SQLite; all optional, defaults work locally) ────────

# SQLite database and Ed25519 signing keys live here (default ./data)
#AQL_DATA_DIR=./data

# Listen address (default :8080). Binding a non-loopback address is REFUSED
# unless LINTEL_BEHIND_PROXY is set — the gateway speaks plain HTTP and must
# not be exposed directly.
#LINTEL_LISTEN=:8080

# External base URL, used for webhook callbacks and for links in messages.
# Required once you connect a chat channel, since the provider has to reach you.
#LINTEL_PUBLIC_URL=https://gateway.example.com

# Set ONLY when TLS is terminated upstream by a reverse proxy. It permits
# binding a non-loopback address; setting it without a proxy in front serves
# the portal and the API in the clear.
#LINTEL_BEHIND_PROXY=1

# 'local' | 'dev' | 'main'
#LINTEL_ENV=local

# ── WhatsApp engine (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────

# 'cloud' (default) — Meta's official WhatsApp Cloud API / WABA.
# 'bridge'          — an unofficial library (Evolution API / Baileys).
#
# WARNING: the bridge path violates KOTVA §26.8.2, which places an
# unconditional MUST NOT on unofficial WhatsApp libraries, and it risks your
# WhatsApp account being banned. It exists because people ask for it. It is not
# the supported path — see site/docs/linking-whatsapp.md.
#LINTEL_WHATSAPP_ENGINE=cloud
#LINTEL_WHATSAPP_BRIDGE_URL=
#LINTEL_WHATSAPP_BRIDGE_API_KEY=
#LINTEL_WHATSAPP_BRIDGE_INSTANCE=

# Channel credentials (WhatsApp Cloud API, Telegram, Slack) are configured per
# account through the portal's Settings screen and stored in the gateway's
# SQLite database — not here. Nothing in this file is a shared secret.

# ── The portal (Vite; VITE_-prefixed vars are PUBLIC in the browser) ─────

# Gateway base URL the portal talks to. Leave unset to get the runtime gateway
# picker, which is how the desktop app finds a gateway on first run.
#VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Mapbox token for the location address autocomplete. Optional — the input
# degrades to a plain text field without it.
#VITE_MAPBOX_TOKEN=
